From 1b80f5b9d5f22c2cc05689b3c265fa92373f0072 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ammar <surfmemo58@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:31:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] 1.6.2: power modes and sensor sources detected per model,
 like LLT

- Power modes from the SupportedPowerModes capability (LLT bit mapping and
  Extreme rules); fallback Quiet/Balanced/Performance on older firmware.
  Published as "Legion Power Modes"; PowerMode rejects unsupported modes.
- Sensors: LENOVO_OTHER_METHOD capability, then LENOVO_FAN_METHOD 7/8 (ids
  from the Linux legion-laptop driver), then the old Game Zone getters;
  ProbeAll includes the fan method reads.
- App and pane build their mode list from the kext (Extreme shows on this
  Legion Pro 5); README compatibility section.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
