@@ -30,6 +30,24 @@ Fixes to upstream code found on the way:
 
 Rapid charge on this Legion is accepted only while the EC flag `QCBX` is set; the kext re-checks it on every battery update and reports `unsupported` otherwise.
 
+## Compatibility
+
+Only the Legion Pro 5 16IRX9 has been tested. The driver is written to adapt to other Legions the way LLT does, but expect differences on other models:
+
+| Area | Other Legions |
+|---|---|
+| Battery conservation, Fn lock, always-on USB | Standard IdeaPad `VPC2004` interface, same as stock YogaSMC. Should work on any Legion. |
+| Power modes | The list comes from the firmware's `SupportedPowerModes` capability (Quiet, Balanced, Performance, Extreme, Custom), using LLT's rules. Without that capability (older Legions) it offers Quiet, Balanced and Performance. Custom only switches to the BIOS's custom profile; there is no editor for power limits or fan curves. |
+| Fn+Q popup | Needs the Game Zone smart fan event (`0xE3`), which Legion firmware sends on Fn+Q. |
+| Fans and temperatures | Tried in LLT's order, first source that answers wins: `LENOVO_OTHER_METHOD` capabilities (Gen 7+), `LENOVO_FAN_METHOD` (some Gen 6/7, untested), the old Game Zone getters (older models). Two fans only; models with a third fan show two. Anything unreadable shows as unavailable. |
+| Touchpad lock, Win key lock, overdrive | Shown only when the BIOS reports support. Touchpad lock may not affect I2C touchpads. |
+| Rapid charge | Only while the EC allows it; shown as unavailable otherwise. |
+| AMD Legions | Same WMI interfaces, untested. |
+
+Requirements: OpenCore with Lilu and VirtualSMC (not FakeSMC), stock YogaSMC removed or disabled, macOS 11 or later for the app and the pane (x86_64).
+
+To check another model, run `yogactl props` (look at `Legion Capabilities`, `Legion Power Modes`, `Legion Sensor Source`) and `yogactl probe`. An issue with both outputs and the laptop model makes support easy to add.
+
 ## Install
 
 Download the zips from the [latest release](../../releases/latest), or build them (below).
